From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Subject: [PATCH] verify native backhaul handovers with targeted topology refresh

A successful native handover response arrives while the controller can still
name the old parent until its periodic topology query. Serving AP queries are
correctly scoped to that old parent, so verification times out despite an
actual successful roam. Request authoritative topology promptly after a
correlated success, with at most three queries two seconds apart. Once that
observation changes parent, request fresh serving metrics without waiting for
the regular cadence. Neither the response nor the requested BSSID substitutes
for native topology or measured link evidence; deadlines remain unchanged.
Include the transaction MID in the verification outcome for wire correlation.

Upstream-Status: Pending

